1.text:
PUBLIC RESPONSE: {C}

The relevant Ontario ESA rules require a written disconnecting-from-work policy and a written electronic-monitoring policy for any employer that has 25 or more employees in Ontario on 1 January of the given year. Both policies must be distributed to every employee within 30 days of being prepared or revised; revised policies must likewise be redistributed within 30 days of each change.

- A, B, D and E all have fewer than 25 employees on 1 January 2023, so neither policy is obligatory and they are compliant.
- C has ~1 000 employees on 1 January 2023 and therefore must maintain both policies. It updates them monthly yet only redistributes the revised versions quarterly. Because a quarterly distribution cycle necessarily exceeds the statutory 30-day window, C is in breach of the distribution requirement as of 2 January 2023.

Thus C is the only employer not in compliance.}

